<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:38Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Black Sea shipping under growing threats as drones hit container ships</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4312374aa0e1bb164428ba5dcff5a1b318ffba8875abe3e6f4c44209d7266b69</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T14:27:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/black-sea-shipping-under-growing-threats-as-drones-hit-container-ships" /><summary type="html">A Greek container ship has sunk after being struck by three drones, potentially of Russian origin, in the Black Sea off the Bulgarian coast on Wednesday, October 28. This incident highlights growing concerns for commercial shipping as the conflict between Ukraine and Russia persists.</summary></entry><entry><title>Spanish transport minister faces calls to quit after deadly train crash</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b73323b28e67f2c350a6ce0617e69abc1f79e6f11e6e023f7ab35a63c13e279a</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T14:21:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-spanish-transport-minister-faces-calls-to-quit-after-deadly-train-crash" /><summary type="html">Spanish Transport Minister Oscar Puente faced calls to resign but ruled out stepping down on Friday. This follows Wednesday’s train crash in Toledo province, which killed 69 people. It is the country’s second high-speed rail disaster this year. FRANCE 24 correspondent Sarah Morris reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Third weekend of protests looms as tensions persist across France</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d49bfe06a72ed5f297d2da96fdf8544c750c6b6687d45964d402c984daf33480</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T14:10:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-third-weekend-of-protests-looms-as-tensions-persist-across-france" /><summary type="html">For the third Saturday in a row, people across France are set to take to the streets to protest against the high cost of living and demand better funding for education. Police are preparing for all eventualities ahead of another weekend of protests, following earlier demonstrations that ended in rioting and looting in city centres.</summary></entry><entry><title>Who is Kevin T., the main suspect behind the racist Trappes attack?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8c9ef56677537fb86b83cfcdeacff6733091ecfca43fd02c390edf5e8b113258</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T14:06:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/who-is-kevin-t-the-main-suspect-behind-the-racist-trappes-attack" /><summary type="html">France's anti-terrorism prosecutor on Thursday released details of the main suspect in the racist attack in Trappes and La Verriere, on the outskirts of Paris, on October 23.The 39-year-old opened fire with a submachine gun, killing 26-year-old Pengo Bossio Wangi and injuring five others.</summary></entry><entry><title>Georgia's European dream left in limbo</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dc2ac13ec2cf83e7af00282a77eaa9852d434726ff650e7a33da1e91a3b6597a</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T13:34:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/revisited/20261030-georgia-s-european-dream-left-in-limbo" /><summary type="html">Two years ago in Georgia, tens of thousands of pro-European protesters rallied against the disputed results of the October 2024 parliamentary election, which was officially won by the ruling Georgian Dream party. A few weeks later, the authorities announced the suspension of the country's European Union accession process. Despite an ongoing crackdown, smaller-scale protests continue every day in the capital Tbilisi.</summary><category term="Revisited" /></entry><entry><title>Russia recruits Africans to fight in Ukraine, families seek answers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fae8b2b3390dd65c3b6b2c2c4f978b8f298755a9f2a0ae7b37722c8d9ea9bc66</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T11:06:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russia-recruits-africans-to-fight-in-ukraine-families-seek-answers" /><summary type="html">While African leaders and Russian officials gather to discuss security, trade and political cooperation at the Africa-Russia summit, one sensitive issue is notably absent from the agenda: the recruitment of Africans to fight for Russia in Ukraine. More than 1,400 Africans have been enlisted since 2023. In Tunisia, concern is growing as the families of several men who travelled to Russia for work or study are still searching for answers about the fate of their loved ones. FRANCE 24's team in Tunisia reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia's bastion of free press Novaya Gazeta shuts down under Kremlin pressure</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:83b58273f5f963a18975ebed2213e458817ba3c3d7d581b908d26a7251934684</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T08:42:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261030-russia-s-bastion-of-free-press-novaya-gazeta-shuts-down-after-years-of-kremlin-pressure" /><summary type="html">Newspaper Novaya Gazeta, one of the last vestiges of independent journalism in Russia, announced Friday that it was closing down, citing pressure from authorities who recently searched the home of its senior editor and earlier this year detained one of its journalists.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine war live: Residents leave Russian-occupied Oleshky in evacuation operation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:516762a7aae2e14caa2d6c588f0a90022d9dbf8d960694e45755555a62a74861</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T07:28:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261030-live-russia-strikes-energy-facilities-kyiv-aid-convoy-heads-besieged-town-oleshky-ukraine" /><summary type="html">Residents evacuated from Russian-occupied Ukrainian town of Oleshky have left for the Russia's Anapa city with a Ukrainian delegation, senior official David Arakhamia said Friday. They are expected to fly to Belarus before returning to Ukraine by bus. Meanwhile, more than 200,000 people remain without power in Ukraine's central Dnipropetrovsk region following deadly Russian attacks. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>French presidential hopeful Édouard Philippe quizzed in embezzlement case</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:447dd445a0a15dee888c0102b2d60f829c9fcce7b864748d5b3eb7f5a4957406</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T06:36:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261030-french-presidential-hopeful-edouard-philippe-quizzed-in-embezzlement-case" /><summary type="html">French investigators on Thursday questioned former prime minister Édouard Philippe, a candidate in next year's presidential election, in a case of alleged embezzlement of public funds. His lawyer welcomed the move, noting that magistrates had chosen not to place the ex-PM under formal investigation.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'Let's reclaim our future': Thousands protest in Italy over rising living costs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3e5a29816bae485f9a616cd72e397abbc7eb343befb6a2f731fcfb9a8feef23a</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T01:53:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261030-let-s-reclaim-our-future-thousands-protest-across-italy-over-rising-living-costs" /><summary type="html">Thousands of protesters marched across Italy on Friday over the rising cost of living, education funding cuts and government spending on defence. Minor clashes were reported in the northwestern Italian city of Turin, while police maintained a heavy presence across the country.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>French shooting suspect deliberately targeted Muslims, Africans</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:db8f6de091a72996f9895f546f5bac4919c4c54fac93692408e89882c4da10be</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T18:45:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-french-shooting-suspect-deliberately-targeted-muslims-africans" /><summary type="html">A man suspected of a gun attack in the Paris suburbs last week, killing one person and wounding seven including a child, has admitted to "targeting individuals who appeared to be Muslim, African, or North African," prosecutors said on Thursday. The attack came amid an increasingly tense political climate, with just six months to go before next spring's presidential election.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ireland becomes refuge for anti-Trump Americans</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0cf1d557c13bf5b2fb6eac912758b998f240d0e516a4cce851cb2da8f28afb59</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T17:08:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20261029-ireland-becomes-refuge-for-anti-trump-americans" /><summary type="html">They have left everything behind to get away from US President Donald Trump's America. Entrepreneurs, academics, scientists and students: tens of thousands of US citizens have moved to Ireland in recent years. Last year alone, some 10,000 Americans settled there and nearly 100 even applied for asylum – citing political, racial or gender persecution.</summary><category term="Reporters" /></entry><entry><title>Aid mission set to enter Ukraine's Oleshky as localised ceasefire holds for third day</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7fb220b5f498f8a4b018d626dc48a932b5f2231d05378cdad902e8af4e7bbe5d</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T16:19:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261029-aid-mission-set-to-enter-ukraine-s-oleshky-as-localised-ceasefire-holds-for-third-day" /><summary type="html">A humanitarian aid mission is set to enter the Ukrainian town of Oleshky, a Ukrainian official said on Thuirsday, as a localised truce between Kyiv and Moscow, brokered by US first lady Melania Trump, held for a third day. Some 2,000 residents in the Russian occupied city have been cut off from essential supplies amid reports that many are starving.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Ireland opens arms to Americans fleeing US President Donald Trump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2340a116ead14bdea61694e25eaaaa03e1bd04483a6814ff44871ff9efb7fd0b</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T15:31:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-ireland-opens-arms-to-americans-fleeing-us-president-donald-trump" /><summary type="html">Tens of thousands of US citizens have fled the United States since Donald Trump's return to power two years ago. Given the language and a shared history, Ireland has been among the top choices for Americans looking for an alternative. FRANCE 24's team reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Real questions to be asked' after deadly train collision in Spain, journalist says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b79bf0d1907a6d3fe2ebfe3592d98ff1efd822f69c80360afbb7c0532d2e336f</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T14:44:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261029-real-questions-to-be-asked-after-deadly-train-collision-in-spain-journalist-says--1490159b0812.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261029-real-questions-to-be-asked-after-deadly-train-collision-in-spain-journalist-says" /><summary type="html">In this edition of Perspective, we focus on the tragic train collision that killed at least 68 people in Spain on Wednesday. We're joined by Nicholas Kingsley, executive editor of Railway Gazette International.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>France: Trappes racist shooting suspect transferred to French court</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e99f03792c2623568fc6020cd37aba129cd139affb7aaf6bd0b253bc41c2a28a</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T13:22:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-france-trappes-racist-shooting-suspect-transferred-to-french-court--154349787262.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-france-trappes-racist-shooting-suspect-transferred-to-french-court" /><summary type="html">French anti-terrorism prosecutor Olivier Christen said the suspect in the Trappes racist attack, which killed one person and injured five others, had been brought before a French court. FRANCE 24 International Affairs Editor Philip Turle has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Very disturbing details': Trappes shooting suspect admits targeting victims by race, religion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bca60c14ae0f30f28f8185464f7308881aa967e6eb4c49210e5e0869c914d66f</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T13:10:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-very-disturbing-details-trappes-shooting-suspect-admits-targeting-victims-by-race-religion--8ff667bcd1eb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-very-disturbing-details-trappes-shooting-suspect-admits-targeting-victims-by-race-religion" /><summary type="html">A man suspected of a gun attack in the Paris suburbs last week that killed one person and wounded five including a child has admitted to "targeting individuals who appeared to be Muslim, African, or North African," prosecutors said on Thursday. FRANCE 24's Charli James reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Spain begins three days of mourning after train crash kills 69</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3fc22abc1a4688fd164e36a44d4a97feef381e19fe8ced5517e5b4aa58d6a867</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T13:01:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-spain-begins-three-days-of-mourning-after-train-crash-kills-69--a6afb8b3d275.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-spain-begins-three-days-of-mourning-after-train-crash-kills-69" /><summary type="html">Spain's second high-speed rail disaster this year, in which one train struck another from behind, killing 69 people, has raised fresh concerns about the safety of the country's rail network ahead of a national election. Three days of mourning have begun in the country.</summary></entry><entry><title>Spain's train crash kills 69 people: What exactly happened?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:efdb54344629cc435de45d9fa6a925f74514b9e037c6943503de0a02293969ae</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T12:53:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-spain-s-train-crash-kills-69-people-what-exactly-happened--724a6701ea5d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-spain-s-train-crash-kills-69-people-what-exactly-happened" /><summary type="html">In Spain, the deadly train accident that killed 69 people and injured scores has once again brought national railway safety under the spotlight. Spain’s transport minister reported an "error" and "inexplicable circumstances" that led to one of Europe's deadliest train disasters this century.</summary></entry><entry><title>At least 13 killed in 'horrific' Russian drone strike at Ukraine train station</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8c3de7cdc326bf4f8d9e92a01bf67529e89d161b25888dd716c727f30ac4ca0e</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T11:36:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261029-at-least-13-killed-in-horrific-russian-drone-strike-at-ukraine-train-station--6f3d27577414.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261029-at-least-13-killed-in-horrific-russian-drone-strike-at-ukraine-train-station" /><summary type="html">At least 13 people were killed when a Russian drone struck a busy railway station in Ukraine's Dnipro on Thursday, President Volodymyr Zelensky said, describing the attack as "horrific" and urging Kyiv's allies not to ease sanctions on Moscow.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>REPLAY: French anti-terrorism prosecutor gives press conference on racist attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b420b906e2728165415b38a2634eacd7f2ab0fc5166a9f4eb2e74b542e8cad52</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T10:56:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-replay-french-anti-terrorism-prosecutor-gives-press-conference-on-racist-attack--d3a956ca5cd8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-replay-french-anti-terrorism-prosecutor-gives-press-conference-on-racist-attack" /><summary type="html">The French anti-terrorism prosecutor, Olivier Christen, gave a press conference on Thursday about the recent racist terrorist attack that killed one man and wounded five others, including a 12-year-old girl, in Trappes. Watch our replay.</summary></entry><entry><title>ECB President Christine Lagarde to step down in February 2027, nine months before term ends</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f885a16a87b968b53e44edd3d1518471428257985bdfc25a5ec702952126a4c3</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T10:21:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261029-ecb-president-christine-lagarde-to-step-down-in-february-2027-nine-months-before-term-ends--9e616059c691.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261029-ecb-president-christine-lagarde-to-step-down-in-february-2027-nine-months-before-term-ends" /><summary type="html">European Central Bank President Christine Lagarde will step down on February 7, 2027, nearly nine months before her term expires, the ECB said Thursday. Her successor will be appointed by the European Council under EU treaty rules.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'Desolation, despair': Spain begins three days of mourning after deadly train crash</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3b4c763a7d2ace5acec20117dfb73343050bc4b1418bf3cc159099028113caf6</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T06:25:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261029-desolation-despair-spain-begins-three-days-of-mourning-after-deadly-train-crash--584ebc479bf5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261029-desolation-despair-spain-begins-three-days-of-mourning-after-deadly-train-crash" /><summary type="html">Spain entered three days of mourning on Thursday after a high-speed train collision killed 69 people and injured scores more. The incident has prompted fresh questions about rail safety and management.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Canada and EU drop associate membership plan in bid to deepen ties</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8306a4cfffd5c6d6ee4ce8222012efc72a38e44be6afbc41dc508c752833267b</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T00:56:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261029-canada-and-eu-drop-associate-membership-plan-in-bid-to-deepen-ties--888df042e229.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261029-canada-and-eu-drop-associate-membership-plan-in-bid-to-deepen-ties" /><summary type="html">Canada and the European Union will pursue closer ties but have dropped a proposal for associate EU membership, according to a joint declaration ahead of Thursday’s summit in Montreal. Prime Minister Mark Carney is seeking to reduce Canada’s reliance on the US, despite warnings from Donald Trump.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Spain rail crash came after train ordered to go in error: minister</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:622e4d0a005e799b7485a1588f96d7e43115b4c33292784c6b07b988a60696b5</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T22:30:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/spain-rail-crash-came-after-train-ordered-to-go-in-error-minister--7fd7d68c2adb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/spain-rail-crash-came-after-train-ordered-to-go-in-error-minister" /><summary type="html">A rail collision in Spain that claimed at least 68 lives on Wednesday came after a train was ordered to go in "error" despite a technical failure that halted all services, the transport minister said. The first findings about the accident in the central region of Castilla-La Mancha are likely to revive questions about rail safety in Spain after another high-speed collision in January killed 46 people. FRANCE 24's James Vasina reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Rail safety questioned after Spain suffers second fatal high-speed train crash in a year</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:31eb041809f1199a8cc501fb14d796fa4f75b739d8b7255471b6cdde92fd9029</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T22:11:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261028-rail-safety-questioned-after-spain-suffers-second-fatal-high-speed-train-crash-in-a-year--9c4ef79853c5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261028-rail-safety-questioned-after-spain-suffers-second-fatal-high-speed-train-crash-in-a-year" /><summary type="html">Questions are being raised about Spain's rail safety as authorities launch an official investigation into the cause of Wednesday's high-speed train collision, which killed at least 68 people and wounded around 100 more, in the country's second fatal rail crash this year.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Amid uncertainty over EU aid, Vitalii Kim insists Ukraine has no choice but to fight for motherland</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0b4c2c4c5daf961d704b4dafb67b71a9893110702b4e75d45c84019a054aca7f</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T19:57:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261028-amid-uncertainty-over-eu-aid-vitalii-kim-insists-ukraine-has-no-choice-but-to-fight-for-mot--388c86d76aac.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261028-amid-uncertainty-over-eu-aid-vitalii-kim-insists-ukraine-has-no-choice-but-to-fight-for-motherland" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Vitalii Kim, Minister for Veterans' Affairs of Ukraine. "If Europe will not support us, we also will fight because it's our motherland," says Kim, insisting that Ukraine's determination to resist Russian aggression will endure regardless of the outcome of negotiations over European financial assistance. Yet behind this assertion of national resolve lies a more complex reality: a country confronting not only the immediate pressures of war, but also its mounting psychological, social and institutional consequences.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Amid uncertainty over EU aid, Vitalii Kim insists Ukraine has no choice but to fight for motherland</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9db80278cfc9fc7c81b0fd7e730d47a5628df98d3f019059525c29677ca798e0</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T19:54:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/amid-uncertainty-over-eu-aid-vitalii-kim-insists-ukraine-has-no-choice-but-to-fight-for-motherland--f23de8cc008b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/amid-uncertainty-over-eu-aid-vitalii-kim-insists-ukraine-has-no-choice-but-to-fight-for-motherland" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Vitalii Kim, Minister for Veterans' Affairs of Ukraine. "If Europe will not support us, we also will fight because it's our motherland," says Kim, insisting that Ukraine's determination to resist Russian aggression will endure regardless of the outcome of negotiations over European financial assistance. Yet behind this assertion of national resolve lies a more complex reality: a country confronting not only the immediate pressures of war, but also its mounting psychological, social and institutional consequences.</summary></entry><entry><title>Spain high-speed train crash kills 68, injures over 100</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e36a5a03bf0672f44900aafa035e23eaf0cc8db19adc66c7d387f8920c38f45c</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T19:32:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/spain-high-speed-train-crash-kills-68-injures-over-100--9e328dc364f1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/spain-high-speed-train-crash-kills-68-injures-over-100" /><summary type="html">A high-speed train collision south of Madrid killed 68 people and injured scores more on Wednesday, with the toll likely to rise, authorities said, in one of Europe's deadliest such disasters this century. The second such accident to strike Spain this year will raise fresh questions about the country's rail safety, with the transport minister speaking of an "error" and "inexplicable circumstances" that led to the collision. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris reports from Urda, south of Madrid.</summary></entry><entry><title>France: Racist attack in Trappes deeply scars local community</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:28b1130ddf841ee4e7d872afa21f00ba0bba97742ec2c548d94c125a7eda3307</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T16:53:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-france-racist-attack-in-trappes-deeply-scars-local-community--369e58b75191.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-france-racist-attack-in-trappes-deeply-scars-local-community" /><summary type="html">It has been five days since a gunman opened fire in the Paris suburb of Trappes in a racist attack that left one person dead and five others injured. Over the weekend, hundreds of people marched through the town to pay tribute to the 26-year-old victim, Bossio Wangi, and show solidarity with his family. The attack has left a deep mark on the local community, and mediators have been mobilised to provide support. Eliza Herbert reports.</summary></entry></feed>
